{{!
    @template tool_vae/roles_install_confirm_page

    The page of the VAE roles when one role is asked for, above the confirmation of the core: what will be created, and
    the list of its rights.

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\roles_install_confirm_page. The template holds
    no logic. Every value is escaped (double braces): none of them is HTML.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * what - string, what will be created
    * rights - array of strings, each right in words followed by its capability

    Example context (json):
    {
        "what": "The role \"Vaeiste\" will be created with these rights, and nothing that exists is changed:",
        "rights": ["Declare one's own experience of an activity (tool/vae:declare)", "View one's own dossier (tool/vae:viewown)"]
    }
}}
<p>{{what}}</p>
<ul>
    {{#rights}}
    <li>{{.}}</li>
    {{/rights}}
</ul>
